{
  "verdict": "supports",
  "report": ".ufo/waves/round-39/w1/C1ScoutProcMounts.md",
  "summary": "proc_pid_mounts(5) says /proc/pid/mounts lists filesystems mounted in the process's mount namespace, and /proc/mounts links to /proc/self/mounts, the process's own namespace. That page defers the format to fstab(5), which names fs_vfstype as the third field. The v7.2 proc.rst states neither claim: it only lists `mounts` as 'Mounted filesystems' (line 778) and gives the separate mountinfo layout (lines 1965-1987). The report holds located quotes, page hashes, a proposed 11-column SOURCES row and a note on id collisions with staged-ids."
}

